rules:
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines semantic contract: distinguish intent vs state, decision vs system
    state, pattern semantics, lifecycle terminology, consistency; global rules are
    hard constraints.'
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in ADR; all other
    representations must be derived from ADR.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: AEM must reflect and not contradict ADR decisions; may include vision/evolution
    items but must not conflict with decisions.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source of architectural planning
    state; generated artifacts must derive planning status from it, not maintain independent
    state.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational architectural primitives, not
    specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must use a structured YAML decision schema with required
    fields; decisions must not be unstructured narrative.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Lifecycle stage of architecture items must be derived from decision status;
    proposed maps to NEXT/REVIEW, accepted may map to DONE, rejected not active, deferred
    maps to FUTURE/DEFER.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR before
    reflected in AEM or other artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts summarize authoritative sources and must
    not become the authoritative source themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern maturity and decision lifecycle are distinct but must be interpreted
    consistently; proposed patterns appear as NEXT, accepted as DONE.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting by default and never directly
    as core.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Global Rules > Project Rules > Prompt Rules; higher precedence rules override
    lower; conflicts must be detected and resolved.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core must be supported by strong evidence, preferably
    from multiple sources or systems.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects participate in shared Knowledge Workspace and must not recreate
    existing workspace-level governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: A candidate signal may only be promoted to a pattern when all mandatory
    criteria (recurrence, impact, reusability, stability) and evidence requirements
    are satisfied.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be proposed by system and explicitly accepted,
    rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Runtime-native workflows must comply with CAS Workflow Execution Model;
    CAS Runner orchestrates, workflows reason, knowledge providers supply knowledge;
    workflows must not perform repository discovery.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
